{
 "_note": [
  "Canonical nutrient vocabulary. Every importer resolves its own labels and codes to these ids; the engine only ever sees the ids.",
  "The ids are the historical engine keys and must stay stable: edges, DRIs, interactions and tests refer to them.",
  "unit is the canonical per-100 g unit the engine assumes. Importers convert into it with ontology/units.py.",
  "infoods is the FAO/INFOODS tagname for the exact definition we store (e.g. TOCPHA, not VITE, because USDA 1109 is alpha-tocopherol). null means no single tagname describes the value.",
  "codes.usda are internal FDC nutrient ids from nutrient.csv (verified in data/ingest/usda_bulk.py). codes.off is the OpenFoodFacts nutriment key.",
  "EU table codes (CIQUAL, Fineli, CREA) are added when their importers are written against the real files, not before.",
  "usda_sum lists FDC components summed into a derived nutrient (omega-3, EPA+DHA). They are not identifiers and are not resolvable as codes.",
  "A codes.usda list with several ids means 'first id present, in this order' (folate: DFE then total; energy; sugars)."
 ],
